Ev4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"American (Traditional), Bars, Cocktail Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":5},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Bars, Cocktail Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"American (Traditional), Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"Tv5gLZyjnMuEpLvdbE5wGw","review_id":"gwe8aBsxieA1oNaoSD_9TA","date":"2019-05-18T02:42:09","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9329983592033386,"text_excerpt":"I've beed to this cute restaurant several times by now. I came here for lunch, happy hour and dinner. Food is consistently delicious, with a nice selection of small plates for a happy hour. Servers are very friendly and attentive, and at the same time not annoying with their attention. They have a beautiful back patio which I've never been at. At this time of the year it's pretty hot outside, but I definitely want to check it out. Parking space is, unfortunately, limited. It was OK for happy hour, but I had a hard time parking for lunch and dinner. Interesting fact about this restaurant is that it used to be a police station. Restaurant is very cute and cozy, you will never tell it used t..."},{"business_id":"Tv5gLZyjnMuEpLvdbE5wGw","review_id":"G5c1YaccwSwmM9kjkXYcmg","date":"2018-07-27T03:09:23","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9255145788192749,"text_excerpt":"I love the food here. It's always unique and flavorful. The environment is okay; it is a repurposed place (jail to restaurant) which at least make it interesting. The prices are very reasonable and the drinks are great. They've got some work to do in establishing uniformly good service (I've been here 8 times and I can say the service can either be great or terrible). My last experience- the young waitress was snotty and rude to my guests and I swore I wouldn't go back after that but I will - the food is amazing :)"},{"business_id":"Tv5gLZyjnMuEpLvdbE5wGw","review_id":"G0F-XU7VfHy5vUt7v5t5CA","date":"2021-05-13T21:39:07","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9248552918434143,"text_excerpt":"I love this spot! It's so tucked out out of the way and rarely crowded (okay I've only been twice but ....neither time was crowded). It's super ADA accessible which is rare in this city. The menu doesn't try too hard because it doesn't have to. The oyster poboy, fried cauliflower appetizer, and peppadew shooters were divine. In fact, my group ordered second plates of those latter apps. Service was fine and largely left us alone, giving us an almost three hour lunch in the sunshine. Patio is smoke free, also a rarity in New Orleans, which I know may be a draw for some!"}],"visual":[{"business_id":"Tv5gLZyjnMuEpLvdbE5wGw","photo_id":"YJi_6SG518eO2YYcga7toA","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/YJi_6SG518eO2YYcga7toA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8932363986968994},{"business_id":"Tv5gLZyjnMuEpLvdbE5wGw","photo_id":"p1gUupnuS2yXnKO8Ih4HgQ",